deliverables stay at their contract paths. Match stored Goal, SPEC summary, or interview restatement to the actual 
request, not just the slug. A different goal receives a distinct folder; uncertain identity needs the smallest 
decision. Preserve malformed, premature, partial, and conflicting evidenceâ€”never delete, overwrite, or silently 
repair it.
Each work's `state.md` opens with `Status: active | frozen | closed`: at most one `active` repository-wide, `frozen` 
preserved as documentation only, `closed` terminal after its report.
The root writes this line on entry and updates it on terminal exit; naming a `frozen` or `closed` work makes it 
`active` and freezes the previously active one, stated rather than assumed.

Every work item governed by this skill requires a Ready SPEC approved by the user. Specify records the user's 
confirmation of the current understanding in state.md before declaring readiness; approval does not replace the 
