95: ## 7. Functional requirements
96: 
97: | ID | Requirement | Priority | Acceptance signal |
98: |---|---|---|---|
99: | FR-001 | A member creates a note in any space of their company with title (required, ≤200 chars), meeting date 
(required), participants (0–50 active company members chosen in a picker), and rich-text content (≤100,000 chars). | 
Must | AC-001, AC-002 |
100: | FR-002 | The rich-text editor supports bold, italic, headings, bulleted and numbered lists, checklists, and 
links; stored and rendered content is sanitized so no script or unsafe URL runs. | Must | AC-003 |
101: | FR-003 | The space detail has a "Notes" tab listing that space's notes, newest meeting date first. | Must | 
AC-001 |
102: | FR-004 | A "Meetings" page lists all notes of the company with search and filters; the dashboard "AI Meeting 
Notes" card links to it. | Must | AC-014, AC-015 |
103: | FR-005 | A note view shows title, date, space (or "Space removed"), participants, content, summary, action 
items, the stored transcript, and access to version history and export. | Must | AC-001, AC-019 |
104: | FR-006 | The author, current participants, and admins can edit a note; others cannot. | Must | AC-004 |
105: | FR-007 | Saving a note that changed since the editor loaded it is rejected with a conflict warning showing the 
newer version; nothing is overwritten silently. | Must | AC-005 |
106: | FR-008 | Every successful save creates an immutable version of title, meeting date, participants, content, and 
summary, recording who saved and when. | Must | AC-006 |
107: | FR-009 | Any viewer can list versions and open an old one; an editor can restore it, which creates a new 
version; action items are not changed by restore. | Must | AC-006 |
108: | FR-010 | The author or an admin can delete a note after confirmation; deletion permanently removes the note, 
its versions, action items, and transcript. | Must | AC-007 |
109: | FR-011 | Note editors create, edit, and delete action items (description required; one optional assignee who is 
an active company member; optional due date without time); editors and the assignee can toggle completion; at most 100 
items per note. | Must | AC-008, AC-009 |
110: | FR-012 | A member uploads a .txt, .vtt, or .srt transcript of at most 1 MB, either to create a new note or to 
attach to an existing note they can edit; a note holds one transcript and a new upload replaces it. | Must | AC-010 |
111: | FR-013 | Empty, oversized, wrong-extension, or unreadable (non-text) files are rejected before any AI call with 
a clear message; nothing is saved and nothing counts toward the daily limit. | Must | AC-011 |
112: | FR-014 | .vtt and .srt cue numbers and timestamps are removed before processing; speaker names are kept. | Must 
| AC-012 |
113: | FR-015 | Before processing, the user sees a notice naming the provider that will receive the transcript text. | 
Must | AC-010 |
114: | FR-016 | The server sends the transcript to the company's configured provider and returns a draft containing a 
summary (key points, decisions, next steps) in the transcript's language and suggested action items with suggested 
assignees. | Must | AC-010 |
115: | FR-017 | A suggested assignee is linked only when it matches exactly one active company member; otherwise the 
item is unassigned. | Must | AC-013 |
116: | FR-018 | Nothing from the AI is stored until the user saves the reviewed draft; the user can edit the summary 
and accept, edit, reassign, or reject each suggested item. Saving stores the summary, accepted items, and transcript 
text and creates a version. | Must | AC-010 |
117: | FR-019 | An editor can reprocess the stored transcript; the result is a new draft for review, and the current 
summary changes only on save. | Must | AC-010 |
118: | FR-020 | If the provider fails, times out, refuses, or rejects the key, the note and transcript remain saved, 
the user sees an error with "Try again", and the attempt does not count toward the limit. | Must | AC-016 |
119: | FR-021 | Leaving the page during processing discards the draft and the attempt does not count toward the limit. 
| Must | AC-016 |
120: | FR-022 | An admin configures provider (Anthropic, OpenAI, Kimi, GLM), API key, model and reasoning level from a 
curated list per provider, and a daily limit (1–200, default 20). After saving, the key is shown only masked and is 
never returned to any browser. | Must | AC-017 |
121: | FR-023 | Without a configured provider, manual notes work normally; AI controls are disabled with "An admin 
needs to configure AI"; admins also see a link to the settings. | Must | AC-018 |
122: | FR-024 | The company's successful AI drafts are counted per day; when the limit is reached, processing is 
refused with a message stating the limit and when it resets. | Must | AC-016 |
123: | FR-025 | Search matches words in title, content, summary, and action-item descriptions, ignoring accents and 
case, in Portuguese and English text, only within the caller's company; filters by space and meeting-date period; 
orders by relevance then meeting date; paginates; shows matched excerpts. | Must | AC-014 |
124: | FR-026 | Export downloads a .md file with title, date, space, participants, content converted to Markdown, 
summary, and action items (assignee, due date, status); the transcript is included only when "Include transcript" is 
ticked. | Must | AC-019 |
125: | FR-027 | Deleting a space keeps its notes; they show "Space removed" and remain on the Meetings page and in 
search. | Must | AC-020 |
126: | FR-028 | A participant or assignee who left the company is shown as "Former member", keeps their place on the 
note, and loses all access. | Must | AC-021 |
