**Section A: Round-1 finding status**

| Finding | Status | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| H1 | Resolved | FR-022 and AC-016 count cancellation after dispatch, matching round 4. |
| H2 | Partially | Atomic admission, crash accounting, and the day boundary are defined. Dispatch retries, refund 
classification, and idempotency lifecycle remain incomplete: N1–N3. |
| H3 | Resolved | Immutable company/creator identity, nullable space FK, company cascade, and conditional legacy 
backfill are specified. |
| H4 | Resolved | Notice revision, admission snapshot, stale-settings rejection, and no fallback are explicit. |
| M1 | Resolved | Pre-change authorization, participant-permission changes, completion-only updates, immutable 
identifiers, and direct-client attacks are covered. |
| M2 | Resolved | Upload persists the note/transcript immediately; generation and Apply are separate states. |
| M3 | Partially | Note/item revisions and atomic Apply are specified, but a draft is not explicitly bound to its 
generation inputs: N5. |
| M4 | Partially | Current membership, historical snapshots, and retained former members are defined. In-flight 
revocation remains unspecified: N4. |
| M5 | Resolved | Append policy, unchecked duplicates, preservation of existing items, and the resulting-total limit 
match round 4. |
| M6 | Resolved | Server-only encrypted storage, client grants/publication restrictions, sanitized errors, and canary 
surfaces are specified. |
| M7 | Resolved | Capability matrix, context/output preflight, truncated-output handling, and a bounded OpenAI latency 
fixture replace the previous unrestricted claims. |
| M8 | Partially | Coverage is substantially expanded, but AC-009 can pass without proving description or assignee 
validation: N9. |
| M9 | Resolved | Required structures, grants/RLS, date-only due dates, legacy-data gate, rollout, readback, and 
rollback are specified. |
| L1 | Resolved | Round 4 explicitly confirms 20/day and midnight Brasília. |
| L2 | Resolved | AC-001 includes today’s note and a backdated note, matching meeting-date ordering. |

**Section B: New findings**

1. **High — N1 — FR-022, §9: SDK retries escape the reservation.**

   **Problem/scenario:** A provider accepts processing, but the connection fails before the response arrives. The 
official SDK retries, producing additional potentially billable dispatches under one reservation. Start-request 
idempotency does not constrain these outbound retries. OpenAI and Anthropic document automatic retries by default. 
[OpenAI Docs](https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/typescript#retries), [Anthropic error 
documentation](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/errors).

   **Evidence:** [SPEC:123](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:123), 
[SPEC:166](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:166).  
   **SPEC fix:** Disable transparent SDK/transport retries. Every additional provider dispatch requires separate 
admission/accounting. Test connection loss after provider acceptance through real routes and DB, asserting the fake 
server’s received-request count.

2. **Medium — N2 — FR-022, AC-016: “rejected without processing” lacks an observable classification contract.**

   **Problem/scenario:** An overload error can occur after an accepted streaming response. Refunding every 
“overloaded/unavailable” error would refund processed work. A fake server’s internal knowledge that processing 
happened cannot establish what the application can infer from the real provider protocol. [Anthropic streaming 
errors](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/streaming#error-events).

   **Evidence:** [SPEC:123](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:123), 
[SPEC:261](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:261), 
[SPEC:279](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:279).  
   **SPEC fix:** Define provider-specific, documented pre-processing rejection signals. Ambiguous outcomes remain 
counted. Clients cannot classify or refund attempts, including through RPCs. Settlement releases a reservation at most 
once against its original day. Tests must use observable production protocol signals, without private “processed” 
flags.

3. **Medium — N3 — FR-022, AC-028: idempotency keys have no scope, payload binding, or lifetime.**

   **Problem/scenario:** A client reuses a key for another note or changed transcript; two callers collide; or a 
delayed retry crosses midnight and a company/day lookup treats it as new. The SPEC does not define mismatch responses, 
pending/terminal replay behavior, or retention.

   **Evidence:** [SPEC:123](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:123), 
[SPEC:172](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:172), 
[SPEC:273](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:273).  
   **SPEC fix:** Scope keys to authenticated company, application user, and operation; bind them to 
note/input/settings revisions. Reject changed payloads. Define replay retention across midnight and crash recovery, 
reauthorize every replay, and distinguish transport retry from a deliberate new “Try again” operation.

4. **Medium — N4 — FR-030, BR-001: removal during generation has no response-time authorization gate.**

   **Problem/scenario:** A member starts generation, an admin removes them while the provider is processing, and the 
pending response delivers company-derived content after removal. Dispatch-time authorization and database RLS do not 
protect that provider response.

   **Evidence:** [SPEC:117](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:117), 
[SPEC:131](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:131); membership removal clears 
company affiliation at [migration:770](E:/projects/virtual-office/supabase/migrations/20260718210827_phase7_company_mem
ber_atomic_removal.sql:770).  
   **SPEC fix:** Recheck current membership and note existence before returning a draft; recheck mutation rights 
inside Apply’s transaction. Discard pending UI results on membership-scope changes. Add a paused-provider test with 
real member removal.

5. **Medium — N5 — FR-007, FR-016, FR-018: the draft’s source revision is unspecified.**

   **Problem/scenario:** Generation starts from transcript T1. Another editor uploads T2; the first browser refreshes 
to the latest note revision. Apply can submit that latest revision with the old T1 draft, passing revision comparison 
while applying stale material.

   **Evidence:** [SPEC:108](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:108), 
[SPEC:117](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:117), 
[SPEC:119](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:119).  
   **SPEC fix:** Snapshot the stored transcript and note revision at generation start; carry that source revision with 
the draft. Apply compares against that revision, even after UI refreshes. Test replacement while the fake provider is 
paused.

6. **Medium — N6 — FR-015/016, §12: v2 adds undisclosed roster export.**

   **Problem/scenario:** Processing an unrelated meeting sends every current employee’s display name to the provider. 
The recorded answer and privacy notice describe sending transcript text, so members whose names are absent from the 
transcript are nevertheless exported.

   **Evidence:** [SPEC:117](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:117), 
[SPEC:233](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:233), [owner 
answer:63](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/state.md:63).  
   **SPEC fix:** Extract suggested names from the transcript and resolve them against company members locally. A 
full-roster transfer requires a separate owner decision and explicit disclosure in the notice.

7. **Medium — N7 — FR-008/029/030, §9: deleted authors and version editors lack a durable lifecycle contract.**

   **Problem/scenario:** An author or historical editor is deleted. The new creator reference has no deletion rule, 
and snapshots cover participants/assignees only. Ordinary FK choices can block deletion, delete company notes, or 
erase historical attribution.

   **Evidence:** [SPEC:109](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:109), 
[SPEC:131](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:131), 
[SPEC:171](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:171); existing editor FK uses SET 
NULL at [baseline:1401](E:/projects/virtual-office/supabase/migrations/20260610183000_baseline_core_schema.sql:1401).  
   **SPEC fix:** Preserve immutable author/editor UUID and name snapshots independently of nullable live-user 
references. User deletion must preserve notes and immutable history. Define rejoin rights by stable application 
identity and test author/editor deletion.

8. **Low — N8 — FR-021, scope: navigation cancellation was weakened without an owner decision.**

   **Problem/scenario:** A user leaves, but processing continues because v2 requires only draft discard. Round 4 
changed counting; it did not revoke the earlier cancellation decision.

   **Evidence:** [SPEC:80](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:80), 
[SPEC:122](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:122), [owner 
answers:91](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/state.md:91), [round 
4:122](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/state.md:122).  
   **SPEC fix:** Require cancellation of the browser request and best-effort abortion of the outbound request, while 
retaining post-dispatch counting regardless of provider cancellation success.

9. **Low — N9 — AC-009: the capacity fixture masks other validators.**

   **Problem/scenario:** With 100 existing items, every attempted insertion fails on capacity—even if description 
length and assignee eligibility are never validated. The acceptance test can therefore pass with those guards missing.

   **Evidence:** [SPEC:254](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:254).  
   **SPEC fix:** Use a below-capacity fixture for invalid descriptions and former/cross-company assignees. Reserve the 
100-item fixture for capacity assertions.

